{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> For — like that darkening and gloom, it shall not be for Jerusalem, against which the enemy oppressed. And some say that the foe shall not be able to fly to Jerusalem, which he oppressed." "<b>As at the first time, etc.</b> For the first time the king of Assyria came, he treated lightly the land of Zebulun and Naphtali, and the last time he treated heavily, i.e., the entire Galilee. And it is possible that גוי [gentile/heavy] is upon Israel, like אחריך בנימין בעממיך (Judges 5:14)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The text reads האחרון but should read האחרונה (feminine, agreeing with פעם); Ibn Ezra's own editorial note צ״ל האחרונה is embedded in the lemma."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:56.414423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}